			<p>
						<table width="95%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" class="border" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#142">Waiting Period For Entrance to CA</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							Greetings and Salutations:<br />
<br />
At yesterdays meeting if you were not able to attend I was made Lead Recruiting Officer.  I thank you and will do the best to bring into the guild good honorable adventurers into CA that will bring glory to the guild, and weed out those that bring dishonor to it.<br />
<br />
After recent events concerning diliberatly killing new guild members and diliberatly not lotoing looted items when in a group fighting, I've decided that some changes on recruiting need to be made.  I proposed a waiting period for enctrance into the guild to the Leaders and Officers yesterday and it was agreed that a one week waiting period be the norm for brand new members.  No more going to the Orc Hill in Kelethin and recruiting anyone and everyone.  All recruits must come thru me first and be interviewed.  I will also communicate with them via email.  This does not, however, mean that your 2ndary characters have to wait the week, they are automatic pending that you have good standing in the guild and so forth.  I want CA to be a strong honorable guild and this method has worked great in the past.  Lots of newbies join guilds just to get pl'd or twinked then once that is done they move on.  If this is all they want from our guild then as soon as they hear of the waiting period they will probably be too impatient to stick around which is good because then the waiting period will have served its pupose.  I am more interested in getting people into the guild that are of high character rather than say we are the biggest guild on the shard but half of us are punks and thugs, not honorable willing to help kind of people, as we have recently seen.  So, if you have a friend that you have been grouped with often and know them to be honorable and good pls give them my email address at Matildauo@austin.rr.com and i will consider them for membership, meet with them, and even assign one of you to fight with them for a few days if necessary.  Lets make CA a great guild and a guild with a good repetation for being Honorable and True.  <br />
<br />
Thank you,<br />
<br />
Sherea  (Lead Guild Recruiting Officer)
						</td>
					</tr>
